{"type": "assistant", "message": {"id": "msg_1785852590595", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "chatcmpl-tool-b094593866295858", "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": "curl -sL \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.24164v1\" -o /tmp/break_abs.html 2>&1; python3 -c \"\nimport re\nwith open('/tmp/break_abs.html') as f:\n    h = f.read()\nm = re.search(r'<blockquote class=\\\"abstract.*?</blockquote>', h, re.S)\nif m:\n    txt = re.sub(r'<[^>]+>', ' ', m.group())\n    print(re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', txt).strip()[:2000])\nelse:\n    print('no abstract found')\n\" 2>&1", "description": "Fetch breaking shortcut learning abstract", "timeout": 60000}}], "model": "GLM-5.2-w4a8", "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0}, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3229f8ec-9185-4188-97bc-2433c848e566", "uuid": "8ff9326e-b0d4-4314-a99d-63ae43dc2170"}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b094593866295858", "type": "tool_result", "content": "Abstract: Recent end-to-end models for EEG-guided target speech extraction report impressive results, underscoring potential for neuro-steered hearing technologies. However, our analysis reveals that high within-trial performance can be driven by trial-specific EEG structure that acts as shortcuts for target selection, leading to poor generalization on unseen trials. To overcome this gap, we propose TRUST-TSE, a two-stage framework to mitigate shortcut learning. By introducing contrastive pretraining with attended-speaker negative sampling, we encourage the EEG encoder to capture fine-grained EEG--speech alignment while suppressing trial-identity cues. We also employ a confidence-weighted extraction objective based on EEG--source similarity to guide extraction using the learned representations. Experiments on KUL and DTU datasets show that TRUST-TSE outperforms end-to-end baselines under strict cross-trial protocols, addressing a key reliability bottleneck of existing approaches.", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3229f8ec-9185-4188-97bc-2433c848e566", "uuid": "bd6f62a6-c5a0-4c03-a769-c07eac2e55b7", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T14:10:05.882Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "Abstract: Recent end-to-end models for EEG-guided target speech extraction report impressive results, underscoring potential for neuro-steered hearing technologies. However, our analysis reveals that high within-trial performance can be driven by trial-specific EEG structure that acts as shortcuts for target selection, leading to poor generalization on unseen trials. To overcome this gap, we propose TRUST-TSE, a two-stage framework to mitigate shortcut learning. By introducing contrastive pretraining with attended-speaker negative sampling, we encourage the EEG encoder to capture fine-grained EEG--speech alignment while suppressing trial-identity cues. We also employ a confidence-weighted extraction objective based on EEG--source similarity to guide extraction using the learned representations. Experiments on KUL and DTU datasets show that TRUST-TSE outperforms end-to-end baselines under strict cross-trial protocols, addressing a key reliability bottleneck of existing approaches.", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"id": "msg_1785852616163", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "关键发现：TRUST-TSE 揭示了现有的 EEG-TSE 模型存在试次特定的捷径学习问题，且在跨试次泛化方面表现不佳。这与 SAGE 声称的稳健性直接相关。让我检查一下 M3ANet 的详细信息以进行公平比较。"}], "model": "GLM-5.2-w4a8", "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0}, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3229f8ec-9185-4188-97bc-2433c848e566", "uuid": "90441a1e-583d-49da-bfde-27450be9176a"}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"id": "msg_1785852616163", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "chatcmpl-tool-b86b980427326bf4", "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": "curl -sL \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.00466\" -o /tmp/m3a.html 2>&1; python3 -c \"\nimport re\nwith open('/tmp/m3a.html') as f:\n    h = f.read()\nm = re.search(r'<blockquote class=\\\"abstract.*?</blockquote>', h, re.S)\nif m:\n    txt = re.sub(r'<[^>]+>', ' ', m.group())\n    print(re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', txt).strip()[:2000])\n\" 2>&1", "description": "Fetch M3ANet abstract", "timeout": 60000}}], "model": "GLM-5.2-w4a8", "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0}, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3229f8ec-9185-4188-97bc-2433c848e566", "uuid": "37810491-695a-410c-b280-f3511fd03569"}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b86b980427326bf4", "type": "tool_result", "content": "Abstract: The brain-assisted target speaker extraction (TSE) aims to extract the attended speech from mixed speech by utilizing the brain neural activities, for example Electroencephalography (EEG). However, existing models overlook the issue of temporal misalignment between speech and EEG modalities, which hampers TSE performance. In addition, the speech encoder in current models typically uses basic temporal operations (e.g., one-dimensional convolution), which are unable to effectively extract target speaker information. To address these issues, this paper proposes a multi-scale and multi-modal alignment network (M3ANet) for brain-assisted TSE. Specifically, to eliminate the temporal inconsistency between EEG and speech modalities, the modal alignment module that uses a contrastive learning strategy is applied to align the temporal features of both modalities. Additionally, to fully extract speech information, multi-scale convolutions with GroupMamba modules are used as the speech encoder, which scans speech features at each scale from different directions, enabling the model to capture deep sequence information. Experimental results on three publicly available datasets show that the proposed model outperforms current state-of-the-art methods across various evaluation metrics, highlighting the effectiveness of our proposed method. The source code is available at: this https URL .", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3229f8ec-9185-4188-97bc-2433c848e566", "uuid": "d1ddeb44-8cbf-47e9-935a-23ec5db3c0d1", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T14:10:36.287Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "Abstract: The brain-assisted target speaker extraction (TSE) aims to extract the attended speech from mixed speech by utilizing the brain neural activities, for example Electroencephalography (EEG). However, existing models overlook the issue of temporal misalignment between speech and EEG modalities, which hampers TSE performance. In addition, the speech encoder in current models typically uses basic temporal operations (e.g., one-dimensional convolution), which are unable to effectively extract target speaker information. To address these issues, this paper proposes a multi-scale and multi-modal alignment network (M3ANet) for brain-assisted TSE. Specifically, to eliminate the temporal inconsistency between EEG and speech modalities, the modal alignment module that uses a contrastive learning strategy is applied to align the temporal features of both modalities. Additionally, to fully extract speech information, multi-scale convolutions with GroupMamba modules are used as the speech encoder, which scans speech features at each scale from different directions, enabling the model to capture deep sequence information. Experimental results on three publicly available datasets show that the proposed model outperforms current state-of-the-art methods across various evaluation metrics, highlighting the effectiveness of our proposed method. The source code is available at: this https URL .", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
